Subject: Beeps on AlphaStation
Date: 1995/09/26
Message-ID: <449ml6$qfc@hermes.acs.unt.edu>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 110855835
distribution: world
organization: University of North Texas
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1,comp.sys.dec


I just got a new AlphaStation 200 4/166, replacing a DEC 3000/300 that
I had been using --- the old machine went to a student, and we did
some hard disk swapping to keep all the files from my old machine on
the new one (basically, the old disk is in the new machine).

The only real problem I have is with the "beep" of the machine ---
it's not very consistent, except in the fact that it always sounds
really bad.  Sometimes it's as little as a light "click" sound, and
sometimes it sounds like I stepped on a cat or something.

I know that the right drivers are installed --- I can make the
multimedia services play sound files, and while they don't sound great
I think they sound as good as they're supposed to with the provided
sound card.

Does anybody have any suggestions of solutions or things I should look
in to?

--
