- - Well, I know what the problem is, but not how to fix it. The problem is one basic to
all DSP chips. The software is blasting stuff at the chip before it's initialized. That's
why you get that weird "clip" sound. Everybody in our group has the same problem. Just
another example of DEC's great software quality. 

