organization: Northern Telecom Inc., Mountain View 
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1,comp.sys.dec

My understanding is that the funky AlphaStation beep is caused by the
fact that the sound card is physically separate from the beep generator.
Since only one of these devices can be connected to the AlphaStation speaker
at at time, some logic is in place to "sniff" the beeper and to force the 
sound card to make some noise when the beeper is triggered.

Jeff Katcher
jkatcher@ntmtv.com

P.S. If someone from Digital can correct me, I'd appreciate it.



