ahabig@bigbang.astro.indiana.edu (Alec Habig) wrote:
>Tony Arnold  <tony.arnold@mcc.ac.uk> wrote:
>>I have a Alpha 200 4/233 connected to a HP Laserjet 4mPlus using the 
>>lpr/lpd protocol. The printer insists on printing a banner page for every 
>>job sent, and nothing I do seems to stop this behaviour.
>>
>>Has anyone else managed to fix this problem? My feeling is that it is the 
>>printer itself, but I guess there may be something I can put in the 
>>/etc/printcap file to solve the problem.

I have now solved this problem by upgrading the firmware on the JETdirect 
card to 3.16. This then gives you a configuration option when you telnet 
in that allows you to turn off banner pages. One problem is that banners 
come back on when you power cycle the printer! I will investigate if this 
is settable via the bootp parameters.

To do this I got the HP download manager from 
ftp://ftp-boi.external.hp.com/pub/networking/software/hpdl0117.exe and 
also the upgrade files. (check out hpdlinst.txt for details). However, to 
make this work I had to configure the JETdirect card via bootp which 
meant loading up the jetadmin package on a local Solaris system here. My 
conclusion was that you could only upload from a host that is in the 
printer's host access control list. It also only seemed to work with the 
community names set to public, but I didn't explore this very far.

