There seems to be a lot of discussion going on about how to duplicate tapes
and whether or not a utility exists to do the dirty work (other than using
dd and guessing at the block sizes).  BSD had/has a utility that will do 
exactly what you're looking for...It is called tcopy.  I got a copy from the
4.4 Lite CD-Rom and was able to complie it without too much difficulty.  I've
used it only a couple of times, but can verify that it works as advertized.
I even used it to copy several IBM/EBCDIC tapes in a strange format and some
HP3000 (MPE/iX) TurboStore tapes that we needed duplicated.  I don't know if
it is publicly available via ftp, etc., but the 4.4 Lite CD-Rom isn't too
expensive and it does have some neat things on it...

