=The UNIX node is called Jacobi, and one of the OpenVMS nodes is called
=NEWTON.  From Newton I can mail a user on Jacobi using addressing of
=the form either Jacobi::user or user@Jacobi.  Similarly, on Jacobi I can
=mail a user on Newton with addressing of the form newtom::user or
=user@newton.  However, if I receive mail on Jacobi (the UNIX node) from
=Newton (the OpenVMS node), then reply does not work.  Let me give two
=examples:
=
=Example 1:  Using SMTP
=1.	As user1 on Jacobi I mail user2@newton
=2.	Mail arrives on NEWTON with message 'New mail on node NEWTON
=	from SMTP%"user1@jacobi.local"'
=3.	From mail on NEWTON I type reply to the message, and this is
=	addressed to SMTP%"user1@jacobi.local"
=4.	Mail arrives on Jacobi
=5.	From mail on Jacobi, I type reply, and this is addressed to
=	user2@newton.local.  I get error message from mailer daemon
=	saying Returned mail: Host unknown, and
=	550 newton.local (smtp) ...550 Host unknown
=	554 user2@newton.local ... 550 Host unknown (Authorative answer
=	from name server)

Unless your network isn't connected to the internet, then the mailer on Jacobi
is misconfigured and/or the mailer on newton is misconfigured.  My guess would
be that you've got sendmail on Jacobi, and that that's where the problem lies.
The sendmail.cf that comes out of the box uses .local as an intermediate step
in parsing and rewriting mail addresses.  It appears that sendmail on Jacobi is
failing to replace the .local with your actual domain (I *THINK* that's
typically done in rulesets 4 and 7).  As a result, you end up with the bogus
.local domain in addresses that Jacobi's dealt with which are in your local
domain.  If further appears that NEWTON has been configured so as to deal with
this problem on Jacobi's part, rather than fixing the problem on Jacobi.

=Example 2: Using DECnet
=1.	As user1 on Jacobi I mail NEWTON::user2
=2.	Mail arrives on NEWTON with message 'New mail on node NEWTON
=	from JACOBI::user1 "User1's account 22-Sep-1995 0845"'
=3.	From mail on NEWTON I type reply to the message and this is
=	addressed to user1@JACOBI.ENET.LOCAL
=4.	Mail arrives on Jacobi
=5.	From mail on Jacobi, I type reply, and this is addressed to
=	user2@local:.newton.  I get error message from mailer daemon
=	saying Returned mail: Host unknown, and
=	550 local:.newton (smtp) ...550 Host unknown
=	554 user2@local:.newton ... 550 Host unknown (Authorative answer
=	from name server)
=
=Sorry about the length of all this, but HELP!, what's going on?!  All the
=other DECnet/TCPIP functions such as SET HOST/dlogin or rlogin seem to work.

Yup.  That's because they don't depend on sendmail, which is almost certainly
where your problem lies.  If all else fails, e-mail me a copy of
/usr/lib/sendmail.cf from Jacobi and I'll see if I can figure out how to fix
your problem.  But please try to have the person who's responsible fix it
first.
