I wonder whether any of you can point me in the right direction for solving
a small problem I have with mail?  I have a cluster of three DEC 3000/400
machines running OpenVMS, DECnet/OSI and UCX (TCPIP), and on the same local
ethernet, a DEC 3000/600 running Digital UNIX V3.2c, DECnet/OSI and TCPIP.

The UNIX node is called Jacobi, and one of the OpenVMS nodes is called
NEWTON.  From Newton I can mail a user on Jacobi using addressing of
the form either Jacobi::user or user@Jacobi.  Similarly, on Jacobi I can
mail a user on Newton with addressing of the form newtom::user or
user@newton.  However, if I receive mail on Jacobi (the UNIX node) from
Newton (the OpenVMS node), then reply does not work.  Let me give two
examples:

Example 1:  Using SMTP
1.	Asuser1 on Jacobi I mail user2@newton
2.	Mail arrives on NEWTON with message 'New mail on node NEWTON
	from SMTP%"user1@jacobi.local"'
3.	From mail on NEWTON I type reply to the message, and this is
	addressed to SMTP%"user1@jacobi.local"
4.	Mail arrives on Jacobi
5.	From mail on Jacobi, I type reply, and this is addressed to
	user2@newton.local.  I get error message from mailer daemon
	saying Returned mail: Host unknown, and
