well as post to the newsgroup.


Martin Farrall


We have just installed (2 weeks ago) an 8200 with 6 CPUs.
It is now on Digital Unix 3.2C.
While it runs fine when it is up (we are trying to get
serious performance measurements done with the help and
support of the Digital joint project at Cern):
The machine crashes once a day with various panics.
The local (german) support appears rather helpless, last week
their prevailing opinion was: software fault, they took the
crash dumps.
Now they believe its a hardware problem, they will change the
memory on Monday.
Our conclusion so far: the smp machinery is a rather sophisticated
one. Unless you have outstanding hardware and software support,
like I experienced it at Cern: Be carefull!
Regards
Walter Brueckner
Max Planck Institut f.Kernphysik Heidelberg, Germany



