>: any company that sells a viewer or mail client for unix that may do
>: this?  it should be able to run under OSF/1 (running X-Windows.)
>
>Let me know if you are successfull.  I have been looking for such a viewer 
>for nearly 2 years now.  The only way that I know to do what you wish is 
>to get a MS Windows environment emulator like SoftWindows or WABI and then
>run either Word for Windows or Word Viewer in that environment.  BTW, both
>Winword and Word Viewer are Microsoft products, but Word Viewer is free!

A company named INSO makes an app for MS Windows named "Outside/In". It's
a file viewer program. Understands a multitude of data file formats (GIF,
JPEG, Word, Excel, Wordperfect, etc.), so you don't have to have the app
which created a data file in order to view it.

INSO makes a toolkit and has an API for ISV's to roll their viewer
technology into an existing app, but they don't have a standalone UNIX
version. I have considered getting their SDK and rolling one myself, but
I'm not sure if there's a market for such a product.

If you're interested send me e-mail and let me know how many copies you
would buy. ;)

Otherwise bug INSO, and maybe do an archie or lycos search on "keypak". If
I remember correctly that's the name of a rival viewer app which just
might have a UNIX port.
