Dave,
	Just yesterday root could not login on the console.  The window manager would
start and a few windows would come up but then everything exited and the login
screen came backup.  dxsession would dump a core.  I finally tracked it to a
typo in root's .Xdefaults.  You might try looking at xdn's config file
(/usr/lib/X11/xdm/xdm-config) and the system Xdefaults file
(/usr/lib/X11/app-defaults/Xdefaults).  On Ultirx machines I found that xdm
behaves bizzarely if there are any typos in /etc/X0.hosts.

I hope this helps.

Andy
