In article <43pph1$m67@happy.cc.utexas.edu> nichols@happy.cc.utexas.edu (Stewart Nichols) writes:


Stewart> I have a TLZ06 tape drive that I have plugged into the back of
Stewart> my DEC 3000 300.  It is recognized as MKA600 at boot time.

Stewart> I can't figure out how to get OSF to recognize the device.  I
Stewart> tried playing aroud with MAKEDEV, but I don't know what
Stewart> device to use.  On one of the other AXP machines there is an
Stewart> identical tape drive and it uses rmt0* and nrmt0*, but I
Stewart> apparently don't know how to tell MAKEDEV the real device
Stewart> name.

There are a couple of things you need to do to get the tape drive into
your system.  First read the man page for 'doconfig' and follow their
instructions for building a new kernel with support for the tape
drive.  Once you have done that, you would:

	cd /dev
	./MAKEDEV tz6

which will make the device identifiers (assuming you have only the one
tape drive) rmt0* and nrmt0* for you.  

John



