Byte order is different from some platforms, but BSD was developed on VAX
processors which have the same byte ordering as the Alpha. PCs are also the
same. Sun and MIPS are not unless it's a Digital MIPS box.

One other, very common problem, is the assumption that a long is 32 bits. I
have to routinely change many variable typed as long to int.

