Georg Umgiesser <georg@lagoon.isdgm.ve.cnr.it> writes:
> The problem lies in the X-server, that continues
>to allocate virtual memory while never releasing any.
>The only thing I can do is shutdown the computer and reboot it.

Nah - just restarting the X process would do the job, too.
See the man pages of init, xdm and X.

	/usr/sbin/init.d/xdm stop; /usr/sbin/init.d/xdm start

Make sure you either issue this as one line or are logged in from a terminal
since there are security issues involved.

>The problem is that after a logout, the server should be reset
>to a clear state. This must be configurable, but I couln't find
>where.

The last line in /usr/local/lib/X11/xdm should read:

:0 local /usr/bin/X11/X -terminate

Hope that helps.


BTW:  It should be fixed by now in the current releases.
