In article <43mq2r$e1r@admin5.hsc.uth.tmc.edu>, jmaynard@admin5.hsc.uth.tmc.edu (Jay Maynard) writes:
|>In article <43mnud$ko9@fstgal00.tu-graz.ac.at>,
|>Thomas Leitner <tom@finwds01.tu-graz.ac.at> wrote:
|>>My advice: Get in touch with your campus license manager and get a
|>>new OSF-USR pak and install it with
|>>
|>>                  lmf register - < osf-usr
|>>                  lmf reset
|>
|>You'll have to do one more thing: delete the OSF-USR license installed with
|>the system. It will take precedence over the newly installed license.
|>-- 

Not necessarily true.

If you obtain an OSF-USR PAK which provides for an unlimited number of users,
you must delete the PAK that already exists.

If you obtain a PAK which provides for a specific number of users, leave the 2
user PAK in as the PAKs will "combine" to give you n+2 users.

Dave



