I have a similar problem with OSF/1, version 2.1. Maybe it is related
to your problem. The problem lies in the X-server, that continues
to allocate virtual memory while never releasing any. It so happens
that after a shutdown, the virtual memory of the X-server is about
8 Mbytes, but after some weeks, I get up to 80 Mbytes. At this point
I get the same warning message as you: 
	"swap space below 10 percent free"
The only thing I can do is shutdown the computer and reboot it.
The problem is that after a logout, the server should be reset
to a clear state. This must be configurable, but I couln't find
where.

To see, if your problem is connected to mine, do a "ps aux" and look
for an entry "/usr/bin/X11/X". Look at the column "VSZ". If this value
is very big, you have the same problem.

