From: warchol@cloud.enet.dec.com ()
Subject: Re: console environ variable PCI_READ_MULT
Date: 1995/09/18
Message-ID: <43k4i9$51@peavax.eng.pko.dec.com>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 110326652
distribution: world
references: <x3pwh4ljvq.fsf@avante.WPI.EDU>
organization: Digital Equipment Corporation
reply-to: warchol@cloud.enet.dec.com ()
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec,comp.unix.osf.osf1


Setting the PCI_READ_MULT environment variable causes the interface between
the PCI bus and the system memory to prefetch read operations. These prefetches
can either help or hinder system performance depending upon the application. If
the system is not likely to use the prefetches data that system performance in 
heavily loaded system may suffer.

Having PCI_READ_MULT on can also increase EISA device latency to main
memory. Certain revisions of the PCI to EISA bridge chip used in the system may
experience latency timeouts with certain EISA devices. It is recommended
you do not turn on PCI_READ_MULT until the soon to be released Version 4.3 of 
the system console code is available in order to avoid any EISA latency timeouts.

Nick Warchol
Computer Systems Group
Digital Equipment Corporation
