Tony Arnold <tony.arnold@mcc.ac.uk> wrote:
>I have a Alpha 200 4/233 connected to a HP Laserjet 4mPlus using the 
>lpr/lpd protocol. The printer insists on printing a banner page for
>every job sent, and nothing I do seems to stop this behaviour.
>
>Has anyone else managed to fix this problem? My feeling is that it is
>the printer itself, but I guess there may be something I can put in the 
>/etc/printcap file to solve the problem.
>
>All advice etc., gratefully received as usual.

My organisation has several OSF/1 machines, which we use for LAN servers
and most of our printing is done using lpd to HP JetDirect Cards. The
problem was very anoying.  Your assumption is correct it is the printer 
itself that adds the page, but it can be disabled if the right options 
are set in the /usr/spool/cfXXXXXXXX file.  The lines that appear in this 
file, are controlled by the options specified in the /etc/printcap file.
The problem is that the :sh: printcap option doesn't have the same effect 
as lpr -h  (Try it for yourself).

There are in fact two fixes to the problem:

1. OSF/1 lpd Patch, DEC have an updated version of lpd available for
   version 3.0 and latter, which correclty understands the :sh: option
   in /etc/printcap.  They shiped the fixed lpd with OSF/1 3.2C, however
   we got a copy for version 3.2 via EMail from DEC TSC.  If needed I can
   supply more info on the exact lpd version, but I don't have it on hand
   just this second :).

2. HP have upgraded the firmware in the JetDirect cards.  They now give
   you a new option to disable the banner page.  You can try and contact
   HP about getting a latter version of the firmware.  It's available
   on the HP BBS here in Melbourne.

Hope that this helps you eliminating those banner pages once and for all 
good luck

Jim Green
Snr. Technical Specialist
ISSC Australia
Utilities Division
Melbourne, Australia
jim.green@secv.telememo.au





