My understanding is that the two numbers quoted (200ns and 265ns) are
for the base 8000 platform and the 8200/8400 systems respectively.  The
base platform can run the system clock up to 100MHz, but the 8200/8400
systems use a 4x clock divider for the 300MHz Alpha, resulting in a
system clock of 75MHz.  This, plus presumably some extra interface
logic for the Alphas (I've only scanned one of the articles) would
likely account for the latency differences.

