DEC's ftp patch server (ftp.service.digital.com) is a joke (as is their WWW 
search engine - I think they reflect one another in terms of available files 
to grab/search)

The last SIX times I tried use the server (we use our registered DSNlink id to 
access the ftp private area) there was some problem or another - usually
related to the batch copy of files to the ftp system failing, which results
in there being close to 0 patches for us to download (there are supposed to
be hundreds). I know several other people who long ago gave up on this service.

Recently, they did some reorg of the filesystem hierarchy (of course, all
the instructions on the ftp server still referred to the old system - sigh), 
when I called them to ask why there were like 2% of the patches available via 
ftp, and why the WWW search engine only matched 'LAT' 3 times :-( they tried to
tell me that they DEC was now merging all their patch kits into much bigger 
chunks (a suggestion which DEC software support later disagreed with)
Finally, after getting pretty annoyed with them, they did some calling around
and admitted there was a problem.

Now, if I need a patch, I just call DEC support 1-800, mail them a kernel
traceback and wait while their support guys figure out the problem and mail me
back the patch - it's frustrating to not be able to be self supporting, but 
it's less frustrating than having to work with the ftp/WWW solution DEC offers.

