I'm not sure where the 20 cycles number comes from (it's not in any of
the documents), but the paper makes clear that the latency of the
memory itself does not vary much with system clock speed (the memory
controller is configurable).  Hence it doesn't seem to make sense to
take a count of 20 cycles and simply multiply it by the cycle time to
get memory latency, as the dram access time is for the most part
invariant with respect to the cycle time.

