Hi there.  I am wondering whether anyone knows about any Dynamic BOOTP
servers which may exist.  Most BOOTP servers are static -- that is, they
have a table of ethernet addresses and their corresponding IP numbers, 
which they give out when BOOTP requests come in.

What we are looking for is a BOOTP server which either has static table
and instead issues IP numbers dynamically from some range of IP addresses
(kind of like Appletalk Fastpath boxes do for localtalked Macs), presumably
ARPing for an IP number before it gives it out to ensure it's not currently
in use.

What would be even better, of course, is a BOOTP server which can do both: 
when a BOOTP request comes in, the server looks it up in a static table, 
and if it finds it, it assigns the corresponding static IP number.  If it
does NOT find it in its tables, it issues a dynamic address as above.

We have so far found one server that does this -- a variation of KA9Q that
runs on a PC/DOS platform.  However, it isn't very stable, and we have yet
