   Presumably this is due to Digitals reduction in the number of
prices for software which occurred last spring. They went from
having a price category for each model line to having a few "Tiers",
such as "desktop system", "departmental system", "enterprise system".
Licences can be transferred between any models of machine within a
give tier. 

   Of course when they did this they set the price for each category to
be similar to what a system in the middle of the range used to cost, so
if your system happens to be at the low end of the new category you get
screwed, if it happens to be at the high end you save. Given that 
there tends to be a lot more low end systems than high end ones I'd
guess that there were more customers who were losers than winners 
under this scheme.

